#X text 240 83 Outputs the total amount of physical memory (RAM) installed
in the machine \, in bytes. To get the size in kilobytes \, megabytes
or gigabytes \, divide the value accordingly.;
#X text 240 153 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 178 • Adaptive resource allocation — choosing buffer sizes
\, polyphony limits or sample-loading strategies depending on how much
memory is available on the machine.;
#X text 250 233 • Diagnostic and monitoring patches — displaying machine
characteristics (together with [system.memused] and [system.hostname])
to identify the machine on which the patch is running.;
